{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789836936,"nonce":"AIA/Ok3ZoKv9dpjIv5Thd2tnzmI=","message":"Decision (user): fuse by default, CLI flag to turn off. Landed in 8ea7747.\n\nEvery engine executes an AIR Fma as one rounding: the interpreter with f64::mul_add, Cranelift with ins().fma, LLVM with llvm.fma; the blanket contract FMF on float arithmetic is gone, so LLVM fuses exactly the peephole's pairs and nothing more. --no-fma clears air_pipeline::fma() before any lowering, which the shared Optimized cache keys on, so it reaches the interpreter, both tiers, OSR entries and --build alike; ASH_AIR_FMA is gone.\n\nVerified on the NUC: interp, hybrid-cranelift, hybrid-llvm, hybrid-auto, jit and AOT all print 22825041 (small) and 112798587 (full); --no-fma prints 22816350 / 112790102 in every one of them, HashLink's values. Parity: MandelbrotSmall/Mandelbrot rows now run no_fma = true against the hl oracle on every tier (the jit_tier = cranelift pins are gone) and MandelbrotSmallFused/MandelbrotFused use oracle_is_interp. aot_smoke gained test_mandelbrot_small.hl. Bench manifest accepts exactly {fused, unfused}. Conformance 1372/1372 on interp/hybrid/jit/aot.\n\nPerf, 9 interleaved reps on the NUC, fused vs no fusion anywhere: mandelbrot full was 5-10% faster UNFUSED in every compiled mode (the fma serialises two independent multiplies; even Cranelift lowering Fma as mul+add paid 7.8% for the peephole's negated-operand shape), nbody hybrid-auto 8.8% faster fused, other nbody rows 5% the other way. A wash; the policy was chosen on semantics, and --no-fma is there for a program that must match hl bit for bit.\n\nSeen on the way, not fixed here: --mode jit --jit-tier llvm fails with 'JIT lost its Cranelift baseline' on any program, on the binary before this change as well.","files":null}]}